  "domain": "infrastructure",
  "definition": "Industrial IoT (IIoT) is the extension of Internet of Things technologies into industrial operational environments, connecting sensors, actuators, controllers, and edge gateways to cloud analytics and control systems in order to enable real-time operational visibility, process optimisation, predictive maintenance, and remote asset management. IIoT integrates historically isolated operational technology (OT) networks\u2014such as SCADA systems and programmable logic controllers (PLCs)\u2014with IT infrastructure, requiring careful management of the resulting cyber-physical attack surface. Key communication standards include OPC UA, MQTT, and AMQP.",
